{number: 151}
{title: God Is Our Refuge Safe}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
God is our refuge safe, strength,
And our present aid, ever near us,
Therefore, tho' the earth be moved,
Hills midst the seas be east,
We will not fear at all, For God is nigh.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Although hills  the nations raged
Although the kingdoms moved, conflicts swelling
Before His mighty word, From war the nations
The troubled earth is stilled When voices is heard.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
O come behold the works,
Jehovah's hand has wrought on the earth here,
To utmost ends of all He causes war to cease
He makes abiding peace in every land
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Be still and bow in fear
And know the He is God All ye nations
To us the Lord of Hosts
ever our refuge be a refuge strong and sure is Jehovah.
{end_of_verse}
